        "content": "\n**Headline finding:** there are **zero test files** anywhere in the repo, and **no test framework is wired up** in either layer — `web/package.json` has no `vitest`/`jest`/`@testing-library/*`, and `engine/` has `pytest` in `pyproject.toml` but no `tests/` directory, no `conftest.py`, no `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`. Before any of the skeletons below can run, both need harness setup (§0).\n\nThe two layers are at very different stages, which changes what \"coverage gap\" means for each:\n\n- **`engine/`** is scaffolding — every pipeline/agent/eval function is `raise NotImplementedError(\"Phase N — ...\")`. Only a handful of pure helpers and the Pydantic models are real. Per `AGENTS.md`, the eval harness is meant to be built *alongside* the engine, so the right move here is **TDD skeletons** written against the documented contract now, so they go green exactly when Phase 2/3 lands.\n- **`web/`** is substantially implemented — most of `lib/`, `lib/server/`, `types/*.ts`, and `app/api/**/route.ts` have real logic, much of it carrying non-obvious business rules (survivorship, auto-apply gating, override validation, versioning locks). This is where undetected regressions are most likely *today*.\n\n---\n\n",
