      {
        "title": "engine/tests/test_generate.py — ground truth generator",
        "content": "from eval.generate import generate, InjectionRates\n\ndef test_generate_is_seeded_and_reproducible():\n    from pathlib import Path\n    m1 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=Path(\"/tmp/run_a\"))\n    m2 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=Path(\"/tmp/run_b\"))\n    assert m1 == m2\n\ndef test_generate_different_seeds_produce_different_manifests():\n    ...\n\ndef test_generate_injection_rates_are_approximately_honored():\n    manifest = generate(seed=1, accounts=1000, out_dir=Path(\"/tmp/run_c\"))\n    reparents = [m for m in manifest if m.conflict_class == \"structural\"]\n    assert abs(len(reparents) / 1000 - InjectionRates().reparent) < 0.02\n\ndef test_generate_includes_genuinely_ambiguous_cases_expected_resolution_escalate():\n    # AGENTS.md: \"That last row matters most\" — a generator with 0 ambiguous\n    # cases makes the paper's escalation metric untestable.\n    manifest = generate(seed=1, accounts=1000, out_dir=Path(\"/tmp/run_d\"))\n    assert any(m.expected_resolution == \"escalate\" for m in manifest)\n```\n\n**Missing error-handling coverage in `engine/` (currently untestable because unimplemented — flag for Phase 2/3):**\n\n| Scenario | Where it should be handled |\n|---|---|\n| Salesforce/warehouse connector auth failure | `connectors/salesforce.py::extract`, `connectors/warehouse.py::extract` |\n| Malformed/missing fields in a raw record | `pipeline/normalize.py::normalize` |\n| `db.py` write functions called with a run in a terminal state | `db.py::write_*`, `update_run_status` |\n| `main.py::execute_run` failing mid-pipeline — does it advance `runs.status` to `failed` with a stage-tagged error? | `main.py` |\n| `agent/graph.py::validate` given an empty string proposal | `agent/graph.py` |\n| `eval/harness.py::run_system` given a manifest with zero entries | `eval/harness.py` |\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "2. Web — pure `lib/` functions (implemented, **zero tests**, highest ROI)",
        "content": "\n```typescript\n// web/lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues, LEGAL_SUFFIXES } from \"./validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"folds case, whitespace and punctuation\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(foldValue(\"ACME INC\"));\n  });\n  it(\"strips a single legal suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme Inc.\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n  it(\"strips two suffixes in sequence (longest match first)\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n  it(\"does not strip 'ltd' out of 'pvt ltd' and leave a dangling 'pvt'\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Something Pvt Ltd\")).not.toContain(\"pvt \");\n  });\n  it(\"keeps the value when the whole value IS a suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\");\n  });\n  it(\"handles empty string\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n  it(\"handles unicode via NFKD normalization\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Söhne\")).toBe(\"sohne\");\n  });\n  it(\"is idempotent\", () => {\n    const once = foldValue(\"Acme Inc.\");\n    expect(foldValue(once)).toBe(once);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"APAC\", [\"APAC\", \"APAC-SOUTH\"])).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"APAC\" });\n  });\n  it(\"accepts a legal normalization of an observed value\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"acme\", [\"Acme Inc.\"]);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Inc.\" });\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an invented value — NON-NEGOTIABLE per AGENTS.md rule 2\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-9999\", [\"ACC-1\", \"ACC-2\"]);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an empty candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"\", [\"ACC-1\"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"   \", [\"ACC-1\"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects when neither side holds a value (both orphan sides empty)\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"anything\", []).ok).toBe(false);\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"anything\", [\"\", \"  \"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"trims the candidate before comparing\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"  APAC  \", [\"APAC\"])).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"APAC\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens both sides and drops blanks\", () => {\n    const row = { a: { values: [\"X\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\"Y\"] } };\n    expect(observedValues(row)).toEqual([\"X\", \"Y\"]);\n  });\n  it(\"returns empty array when both sides are empty (orphan/orphan — should not occur, but must not throw)\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [] }, b: { values: [] } })).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/diff-chars.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { diffSegments } from \"./diff-chars\";\n\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"equal values put everything in prefix, nothing emphasized\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"suffix differs: APAC vs APAC-SOUTH\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC-SOUTH\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"-SOUTH\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"prefix differs: ACC-4417 vs ACC-2201 (shared '-' boundary, differing digits)\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\");\n    expect(result.prefix).toBe(\"ACC-\");\n  });\n  it(\"middle differs with shared head and tail\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"A-x-B\", \"A-y-B\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"A-\", middle: \"x\", suffix: \"-B\" });\n  });\n  it(\"completely different strings — prefix and suffix both empty\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"Acme\", \"Zenith\");\n    expect(result.prefix).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n  it(\"one empty string\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"both empty strings — equal, not a crash\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"\", \"\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n  it(\"case-sensitivity: 'Acme Inc.' vs 'ACME INC' — cosmetic conflict must still light up\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"Acme Inc.\", \"ACME INC\");\n    expect(result.middle.length).toBeGreaterThan(0); // not byte-identical, so something must differ\n  });\n  it(\"prefix and suffix never overlap (regression guard for the two-pointer bound)\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"aa\", \"aaa\");\n    expect(result.prefix.length + result.suffix.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(2);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/format.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  shortRunId, formatElapsed, formatCount, formatStat,\n  formatClockTime, formatTimestamp, formatRelative, formatConfidence,\n} from \"./format\";\n\ndescribe(\"shortRunId\", () => {\n  it(\"strips hyphens and uses interpunct separator\", () => {\n    expect(shortRunId(\"a41f0000-c9aa-0000-0000-000000000000\")).toBe(\"a41f·00\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatElapsed\", () => {\n  it(\"mm:ss under an hour\", () => expect(formatElapsed(65_000)).toBe(\"01:05\"));\n  it(\"h:mm:ss over an hour\", () => expect(formatElapsed(3_665_000)).toBe(\"1:01:05\"));\n  it(\"zero\", () => expect(formatElapsed(0)).toBe(\"00:00\"));\n  it(\"negative ms clamps to zero instead of throwing\", () => expect(formatElapsed(-500)).toBe(\"00:00\"));\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatStat\", () => {\n  it(\"null renders em dash, not zero\", () => expect(formatStat(null)).toBe(\"—\"));\n  it(\"undefined renders em dash\", () => expect(formatStat(undefined)).toBe(\"—\"));\n  it(\"zero renders as '0', distinct from unknown\", () => expect(formatStat(0)).toBe(\"0\"));\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatConfidence\", () => {\n  it(\"always two decimals\", () => expect(formatConfidence(0.9)).toBe(\"0.90\"));\n  it(\"never a percentage\", () => expect(formatConfidence(1)).toBe(\"1.00\"));\n  it(\"boundary zero\", () => expect(formatConfidence(0)).toBe(\"0.00\"));\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatRelative\", () => {\n  const now = new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:00:00Z\");\n  it(\"just now under a minute\", () => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:59:30Z\"), now)).toBe(\"just now\");\n  });\n  it(\"minutes\", () => expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:55:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"5m ago\"));\n  it(\"hours\", () => expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T09:00:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"3h ago\"));\n  it(\"days\", () => expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-06T12:00:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"2d ago\"));\n  it(\"future date (clock skew) does not throw or go negative-nonsensical\", () => {\n    expect(() => formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:05:00Z\"), now)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/rule-trace.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { deriveRuleTrace } from \"./rule-trace\";\n\ndescribe(\"deriveRuleTrace\", () => {\n  it(\"no resolution yet: single not-yet-resolved classify step\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(makeRow({ resolution: null }));\n    expect(trace).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect(trace[0].ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rule decided: classify + apply ran, propose + validate reflect it\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(makeRow({\n      resolution: makeResolution({ appliedRuleId: \"r1\", proposedValue: \"APAC\" }),\n    }));\n    expect(trace.find(s => s.node === \"apply\")!.ran).toBe(true);\n    expect(trace.find(s => s.node === \"propose\")!.ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"no rule matched, model proposed: propose ran, apply did not\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(makeRow({\n      resolution: makeResolution({ appliedRuleId: null, proposedValue: \"APAC\" }),\n    }));\n    expect(trace.find(s => s.node === \"propose\")!.ran).toBe(true);\n    expect(trace.find(s => s.node === \"apply\")!.ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"escalated with no proposed value: validate did not run (nothing to check)\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(makeRow({\n      resolution: makeResolution({ appliedRuleId: null, proposedValue: \"\" }),\n    }));\n    expect(trace.find(s => s.node === \"validate\")!.ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/audit-detail.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { auditDetailParts, auditDetailLine, auditNote } from \"./audit-detail\";\n\ndescribe(\"auditDetailParts\", () => {\n  it(\"unrecognized detail keys produce an empty array, not a stray dot\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(makeEntry({ detail: { totallyUnknown: \"x\" } }))).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"shows both proposed and chosen value when they differ (override)\", () => {\n    const parts = auditDetailParts(makeEntry({\n      detail: { proposedValue: \"APAC\", chosenValue: \"APAC-SOUTH\" },\n    }));\n    expect(parts).toContain(\"APAC → APAC-SOUTH\");\n  });\n  it(\"shows just chosen value when proposed equals chosen (approve)\", () => {\n    const parts = auditDetailParts(makeEntry({\n      detail: { proposedValue: \"APAC\", chosenValue: \"APAC\" },\n    }));\n    expect(parts.some(p => p.includes(\"→\"))).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"count noun depends on action type\", () => {\n    const detected = auditDetailParts(makeEntry({ action: \"conflict_detected\", detail: { count: 12 } }));\n    const applied = auditDetailParts(makeEntry({ action: \"auto_applied\", detail: { count: 12 } }));\n    expect(detected.join()).toContain(\"conflicts\");\n    expect(applied.join()).toContain(\"resolutions\");\n  });\n  it(\"previousStatus renders underscores as hyphens\", () => {\n    const parts = auditDetailParts(makeEntry({ detail: { previousStatus: \"auto_applied\" } }));\n    expect(parts).toContain(\"was auto-applied\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"auditDetailLine\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (not empty string) when nothing recognized\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailLine(makeEntry({ detail: {} }))).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"auditNote\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when no note key present\", () => {\n    expect(auditNote(makeEntry({ detail: {} }))).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/reviewer-label.test.ts + web/lib/uuid.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewerLabel } from \"./reviewer-label\";\nimport { isUuid } from \"./uuid\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers username over email\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j.rao\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to email when username is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j@x.com\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to the given fallback when user is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel(null, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back when both username and email are missing\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: null }, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isUuid\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts a well-formed v4 uuid\", () => expect(isUuid(\"a41f0000-c9aa-4000-8000-000000000000\")).toBe(true));\n  it(\"rejects a non-uuid route param ('banana')\", () => expect(isUuid(\"banana\")).toBe(false));\n  it(\"rejects a uuid missing a segment\", () => expect(isUuid(\"a41f0000-c9aa-4000-8000\")).toBe(false));\n  it(\"is case-insensitive\", () => expect(isUuid(\"A41F0000-C9AA-4000-8000-000000000000\")).toBe(true));\n  it(\"rejects empty string\", () => expect(isUuid(\"\")).toBe(false));\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "3. Web — `types/*.ts` business-rule functions",
        "content": "\n```typescript\n// web/types/run.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { isTerminalRunStatus, runStageIndex, isStatKnown, failedStage } from \"./run\";\n\ndescribe(\"isTerminalRunStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"complete and failed are terminal\", () => {\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"complete\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"failed\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"every in-flight status is not terminal\", () => {\n    for (const s of [\"queued\", \"extracting\", \"matching\", \"detecting\", \"resolving\"] as const) {\n      expect(isTerminalRunStatus(s)).toBe(false);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isStatKnown\", () => {\n  it(\"a stat produced by a future stage is unknown while queued\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"queued\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"a stat becomes known once its producing stage is behind current\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"entitiesA\", \"matching\")).toBe(true); // produced by 'extracting'\n  });\n  it(\"a stat is NOT known while its own producing stage is still running\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"matching\")).toBe(false); // matching hasn't finished yet\n  });\n  it(\"all stats known once complete\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"tokensUsed\", \"complete\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"all stats known (whatever was computed) once failed — partial numbers still shown\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"conflicts\", \"failed\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"failedStage\", () => {\n  it(\"parses 'stage=extract' convention\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"source=Databricks GTM stage=extract\")).toBe(\"extracting\");\n  });\n  it(\"parses stage=dispatch as queued\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"EngineDispatch: timeout\\nstage=dispatch\")).toBe(\"queued\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when error has no stage= marker\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"Connection refused\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when error is null\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(null)).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null for an unrecognized stage verb\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"stage=teleporting\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"is case-insensitive on the stage verb\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"stage=EXTRACT\")).toBe(\"extracting\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/types/rules.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ruleSpecificity, orderRulesByEvaluation, survivorshipRuleSchema } from \"./rules\";\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  it(\"wildcard/wildcard is least specific (0)\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" } as any)).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"exact/exact is most specific (3)\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ field: \"territory\", entityType: \"account\" } as any)).toBe(3);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"orderRulesByEvaluation\", () => {\n  it(\"sorts most specific first\", () => {\n    const wildcard = { id: \"w\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" } as any;\n    const specific = { id: \"s\", field: \"territory\", entityType: \"account\" } as any;\n    const ordered = orderRulesByEvaluation([wildcard, specific]);\n    expect(ordered[0].id).toBe(\"s\");\n  });\n  it(\"stable sort: equal specificity keeps author order\", () => {\n    const r1 = { id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" } as any;\n    const r2 = { id: \"r2\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" } as any;\n    expect(orderRulesByEvaluation([r1, r2]).map(r => r.id)).toEqual([\"r1\", \"r2\"]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts escalate strategy without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"escalate\", description: \"x\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/types/queue.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { conflictFieldLabel, severityReason, queueQuerySchema } from \"./queue\";\n\ndescribe(\"conflictFieldLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"orphan reads 'entity absent' regardless of field name\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"territory\", conflictClass: \"orphan\", a: {values:[],present:false}, b:{values:[],present:true} })).toBe(\"entity absent\");\n  });\n  it(\"duplicate shows 'N → M' when counts differ\", () => {\n    const label = conflictFieldLabel({\n      field: \"x\", conflictClass: \"duplicate\",\n      a: { values: [\"1\", \"2\"], present: true }, b: { values: [\"1\"], present: true },\n    });\n    expect(label).toBe(\"2 → 1\");\n  });\n  it(\"duplicate falls back to generic label when to-count is 0\", () => {\n    const label = conflictFieldLabel({\n      field: \"x\", conflictClass: \"duplicate\",\n      a: { values: [\"1\", \"2\"], present: true }, b: { values: [], present: false },\n    });\n    expect(label).toBe(\"duplicate record\");\n  });\n  it(\"attribute/structural/cosmetic show the raw field name\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"territory\", conflictClass: \"attribute\", a:{values:[],present:true}, b:{values:[],present:true} })).toBe(\"territory\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"queueQuerySchema\", () => {\n  it(\"parses comma-separated severities into numbers, dropping invalid ones\", () => {\n    const result = queueQuerySchema.parse({ severities: \"4,3,99,abc\" });\n    expect(result.severities).toEqual([4, 3]);\n  });\n  it(\"defaults status to 'escalated'\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({}).status).toBe(\"escalated\");\n  });\n  it(\"defaults page to 1 and coerces string input\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({ page: \"3\" }).page).toBe(3);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects page 0 or negative\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.safeParse({ page: \"0\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"empty severities string yields empty array, not [NaN]\", () => {\n    expect(queueQuerySchema.parse({ severities: \"\" }).severities).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "4. Web — `lib/server/*` (DB-integration + engine-HTTP client)",
        "content": "\nTwo different testing strategies apply here:\n\n- **`engine.ts`** has no DB dependency — pure `fetch` — mock `fetch` with `vi.stubGlobal`.\n- Everything else touches Postgres via Drizzle — needs either a real test database (`docker` Postgres + migrations) or `pg-mem`/testcontainers. **This is a gap even at the infra level** — recommend a `web/tests/db.ts` helper that spins up a throwaway schema per test run.\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/server/engine.test.ts — no DB needed, mock fetch\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { startRun, fetchEngineStatus, EngineUnreachableError } from \"./engine\";\n\ndescribe(\"startRun\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => { process.env.ENGINE_URL = \"http://engine.test\"; vi.restoreAllMocks(); });\n\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when fetch rejects (network down)\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error(\"ECONNREFUSED\")));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toBeInstanceOf(EngineUnreachableError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws with timeout-specific message when the request times out\", async () => {\n    const err = new Error(\"timeout\"); err.name = \"TimeoutError\";\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(err));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toThrow(/no response within/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when engine responds non-2xx\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"bad\", { status: 500 })));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toBeInstanceOf(EngineUnreachableError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when engine returns 200 with a body that fails the tool-contract schema\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(Response.json({ wrong: \"shape\" })));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toThrow(/unexpected body/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError (not a generic Error) when ENGINE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    delete process.env.ENGINE_URL;\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toBeInstanceOf(EngineUnreachableError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"resolves silently on a valid 200 response\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(Response.json({ runId: \"run-1\", accepted: true })));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).resolves.toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"fetchEngineStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (never throws) when the engine is unreachable — polling must degrade gracefully\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error(\"down\")));\n    await expect(fetchEngineStatus(\"run-1\")).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null on a non-2xx response\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(\"\", { status: 503 })));\n    expect(await fetchEngineStatus(\"run-1\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when the body fails schema validation\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(Response.json({ garbage: true })));\n    expect(await fetchEngineStatus(\"run-1\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/server/export.test.ts — decisionsToCsv and estimateExportBytes are PURE, test directly\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { decisionsToCsv, estimateExportBytes, isExportSection } from \"./export\";\n\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv\", () => {\n  it(\"escapes a value containing a comma\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([makeDecision({ entityName: \"Acme, Inc.\" })]);\n    expect(csv).toContain('\"Acme, Inc.\"');\n  });\n  it(\"escapes a value containing a double quote by doubling it\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([makeDecision({ rationale: 'Said \"APAC\"' })]);\n    expect(csv).toContain('\"\"APAC\"\"');\n  });\n  it(\"escapes a value containing a newline\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([makeDecision({ rationale: \"line1\\nline2\" })]);\n    expect(csv.split(\"\\r\\n\").length).toBeGreaterThan(2); // the embedded \\n must stay inside one quoted cell\n  });\n  it(\"renders null as empty cell, not the string 'null'\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([makeDecision({ status: null })]);\n    expect(csv).not.toContain(\"null\");\n  });\n  it(\"ends with a trailing CRLF\", () => {\n    expect(decisionsToCsv([makeDecision()])).toMatch(/\\r\\n$/);\n  });\n  it(\"empty input still produces a header row\", () => {\n    expect(decisionsToCsv([]).trim().split(\"\\r\\n\")).toHaveLength(1);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"estimateExportBytes\", () => {\n  it(\"sums only the requested sections\", () => {\n    const sizing = { hierarchy: 10, decisions: 5, orphans: 2, stats: 1 };\n    const bytes = estimateExportBytes(sizing, [\"decisions\"]);\n    expect(bytes).toBe(5 * 640);\n  });\n  it(\"empty sections list returns 0\", () => {\n    expect(estimateExportBytes({ hierarchy: 10, decisions: 5, orphans: 2, stats: 1 }, [])).toBe(0);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"isExportSection\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts a known section\", () => expect(isExportSection(\"hierarchy\")).toBe(true));\n  it(\"rejects an unknown string\", () => expect(isExportSection(\"bogus\")).toBe(false));\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/server/conflicts.ts::recordReview` — the highest-value integration-test target in the whole repo.** It encodes the reviewer/audit/validate-value business rules together; a unit test on the pieces isn't enough because the bug surface is in how they compose against real rows.\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/server/conflicts.integration.test.ts — requires a seeded test DB\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { recordReview, getReviewTarget } from \"./conflicts\";\n// import { withTestDb, seedConflictAndResolution } from \"@/tests/db\"; // infra TODO\n\ndescribe(\"recordReview\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 404 for a conflict id that does not exist\", async () => {\n    const result = await recordReview({ conflictId: crypto.randomUUID(), action: { action: \"approve\" }, reviewer: r() });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, code: 404, message: expect.any(String) });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 409 approving a conflict with no resolution yet (run still resolving)\", async () => {\n    // seed a conflict with resolutionId = null\n    const result = await recordReview({ conflictId: \"seeded-unresolved\", action: { action: \"approve\" }, reviewer: r() });\n    expect(result).toMatchObject({ ok: false, code: 409 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 409 approving a conflict whose rule said escalate (empty proposedValue)\", async () => {\n    // seed resolution with proposedValue: \"\", status: \"escalated\"\n    const result = await recordReview({ conflictId: \"seeded-escalated-empty\", action: { action: \"approve\" }, reviewer: r() });\n    expect(result).toMatchObject({ ok: false, code: 409 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 400 overriding with a value that is neither observed value nor a legal normalization\", () => {});\n\n  it(\"override stores the OBSERVED value the candidate folds onto, not the typed string\", () => {});\n\n  it(\"approve writes status='approved' and appends a human_approved audit row with previousStatus\", () => {});\n\n  it(\"reject writes status='rejected' and audit detail has chosenValue=null (nothing was applied)\", () => {});\n\n  it(\"does NOT modify proposedValue, rationale, confidence, or appliedRuleId on any action\", () => {});\n\n  it(\"moving from override back to approve clears overrideValue on the row\", () => {});\n\n  it(\"audit detail includes previousStatus equal to the status BEFORE this call\", () => {});\n\n  it(\"reviewedBy always comes from the passed reviewer, never from the action payload\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/server/rulesets.integration.test.ts\ndescribe(\"createRulesetVersion\", () => {\n  it(\"first save of a new policy name starts at version 1\", () => {});\n  it(\"second save of the same name increments to the previous max + 1\", () => {});\n  it(\"the newly created version becomes isActive=true and the prior active version becomes false\", () => {});\n  it(\"only one ruleset is active across ALL names after a save (not just this name)\", () => {});\n  it(\"two concurrent saves of the same policy name never produce the same version number (advisory lock)\", () => {\n    // regression test for the pg_advisory_xact_lock — run two calls with Promise.all\n  });\n  it(\"a prior version's rules are unchanged and still readable after a new version is saved\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/server/runs.integration.test.ts\ndescribe(\"getLatestRunWithConflicts\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when no runs exist\", () => {});\n  it(\"skips a more-recent run that has zero conflicts in favor of an older one that has some\", () => {});\n});\ndescribe(\"failUndispatchedRun\", () => {\n  it(\"only updates a run whose status is still 'queued' (guard against overwriting engine progress)\", () => {});\n  it(\"no-ops silently when the run has already moved past 'queued'\", () => {});\n});\ndescribe(\"getSeverityBreakdown\", () => {\n  it(\"drops a row whose severity is outside 1..4 rather than widening the histogram\", () => {});\n  it(\"returns EMPTY_SEVERITY_BREAKDOWN (not throwing) for a run with zero conflicts\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/server/entities.integration.test.ts\ndescribe(\"countChildrenByParent\", () => {\n  it(\"returns an empty map for an empty externalIds array without hitting the DB\", () => {});\n  it(\"de-duplicates externalIds before querying\", () => {});\n  it(\"keys results by sourceId:externalId so the same external id on two sources doesn't collide\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "5. Web — API routes (`app/api/**/route.ts`)",
        "content": "\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/runs/route.test.ts — integration, through the real handler\ndescribe(\"POST /api/runs\", () => {\n  it(\"401s when unauthenticated\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId === sourceBId (self-reconciliation guard)\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s with 'Source A no longer exists' when sourceAId is a valid uuid but not in the DB\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s with 'That ruleset version no longer exists' when rulesetId is stale\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s when the body is not valid JSON\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s when the body is missing a required field, with field-addressable issues in the response\", () => {});\n  it(\"201s and appends a run_started audit row with sourceAId/sourceBId/rulesetVersion in detail\", () => {});\n  it(\"when the engine is unreachable: still 201s, marks the run failed with stage=dispatch, and appends run_failed audit\", () => {});\n  it(\"actor on the audit row is the authenticated reviewer's label, never a value from the request body\", () => {});\n});\n\ndescribe(\"GET /api/runs\", () => {\n  it(\"401s when unauthenticated\", () => {});\n  it(\"200s with { runs: [] } when there are no runs\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"PATCH /api/conflicts/:conflictId/resolution\", () => {\n  it(\"404s for a non-uuid conflictId param (route smuggling / malformed id)\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s for a body missing 'action'\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s for action=override with overrideValue as an empty string (schema min length)\", () => {});\n  it(\"401s when unauthenticated, BEFORE the body is parsed or the DB is touched\", () => {});\n  it(\"the response never echoes back a client-supplied reviewedBy\", () => {});\n  it(\"propagates recordReview's { ok:false, code, message } to the correct HTTP status\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/runs/[runId]/export/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"GET /api/runs/:runId/export\", () => {\n  it(\"400s on an unrecognized format (?format=xml)\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s on an unknown section name (?sections=hierarchy,bogus)\", () => {});\n  it(\"404s for a well-formed but nonexistent runId\", () => {});\n  it(\"404s for a non-uuid runId before any DB query\", () => {});\n  it(\"csv format ignores the hierarchy/orphans/stats sections and returns only decisions\", () => {});\n  it(\"json format with no ?sections= defaults to hierarchy+decisions only\", () => {});\n  it(\"filename in Content-Disposition strips the interpunct from shortRunId\", () => {});\n  it(\"two requests with the same sections in different order produce byte-identical files (canonical ordering)\", () => {});\n  it(\"401s when unauthenticated\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/sources/route.test.ts + rulesets/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"POST /api/sources\", () => {\n  it(\"401s when unauthenticated\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s on invalid body (createSourceSchema failure)\", () => {});\n  it(\"cannot accept any field that could carry a credential — schema-level regression guard\", () => {\n    // assert createSourceSchema has no 'password'/'token'/'secret' key path even if sent\n  });\n});\ndescribe(\"POST /api/rulesets\", () => {\n  it(\"400s when rules array is empty (schema .min(1))\", () => {});\n  it(\"400s when a rule has strategy=prefer_source with no preferredSourceId\", () => {});\n  it(\"201s and the new version is immediately returned as isActive=true\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/_lib/respond.test.ts\ndescribe(\"parseJson\", () => {\n  it(\"returns ok:false with 400 when body is not JSON\", () => {});\n  it(\"returns field-addressable issues keyed by dotted path on schema failure\", () => {});\n  it(\"nested field errors use '.' joined paths (e.g. 'config.objects')\", () => {});\n  it(\"a top-level (non-field) issue is keyed under '_'\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "6. Missing error-handling coverage — summary",
        "content": "\n| Area | Untested failure mode | Risk if it regresses |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lib/server/engine.ts` | Engine down at dispatch time | Run silently stuck in `queued` forever (the exact \"worst outcome\" `AGENTS.md` calls out) |\n| `lib/server/conflicts.ts::recordReview` | Approving an escalated conflict with no proposal | A reviewer's click could write a bogus \"approved\" status with nothing behind it |\n| `lib/server/rulesets.ts::createRulesetVersion` | Concurrent saves of the same ruleset name | Two rows could get the same version number without the advisory lock — breaks reproducibility guarantee |\n| `app/api/runs/route.ts` | `sourceAId === sourceBId` | A meaningless self-reconciling run silently \"succeeds\" |\n| `app/api/runs/[runId]/export/route.ts` | Unknown `?sections=` value | Currently 400s — verify it stays that way, not a silent drop |\n| `lib/validate-value.ts::checkObservedValue` | Both sides empty (double-orphan, shouldn't occur) | Must not throw; must reject cleanly |\n| engine `agent/graph.py::validate` | Hallucinated value from the model | This is rule 2 in `AGENTS.md` — \"non-negotiable\" — currently has zero test coverage because it's unimplemented |\n| engine `db.py::update_run_status` | Called with source/ruleset columns | Should be structurally impossible (no params for them) — worth a type-level test once implemented |\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "7. Integration test gaps (cross-layer)",
        "content": "\n1. **Web ↔ Engine contract drift.** `types/run.ts::engineStartRunResponseSchema`/`engineRunStatusSchema` and `pipeline/schema.py::StartRunResponse`/`RunStatusResponse` must stay byte-identical. No test currently enforces this. Recommend a **contract test**: generate a sample payload from the Pydantic model (`model_dump(by_alias=True)`), and assert the Zod schema on the TS side accepts it, in CI, on every PR that touches either file.\n2. **Full pipeline run, engine only.** Once Phase 1–3 land: `extract → normalize → block/match → detect → resolve` against `eval/generate.py` synthetic output, asserting `engine/eval/harness.py` metrics are computable end to end (currently impossible — nothing is implemented).\n3. **`recordReview` → `getQueuePage` round trip.** After a review action, does the same conflict disappear from the `escalated` filter and appear under `all`? No test spans both read and write paths in `conflicts.ts` together.\n4. **Auth boundary end-to-end.** `proxy.ts` + `requireReviewerForApi` + `requireReviewer` — is there any route reachable without a session? `AGENTS.md`'s own comment in `auth.ts` documents a past bug class here (matcher/resolution divergence); this deserves an integration test that enumerates every `app/api/**/route.ts` and asserts each exported handler 401s unauthenticated, rather than relying on each route remembering to call the gate.\n5. **Export round-trip.** `buildRunExport` → `decisionsToCsv` — does a decision row survive JSON export and CSV export with the same `appliedValue` derivation? No test compares the two formats for the same run.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Priority order",
        "content": "1. Wire up `vitest` + `pytest` config (§0) — nothing else is runnable without it.\n2. `web/lib/*.ts` pure functions (§2) — implemented, zero-risk to add, highest bug-catching density per line of test.\n3. `engine` implemented helpers + `pipeline/schema.py` validators (§1a) — same reasoning, other side of the boundary.\n4. `recordReview` and `createRulesetVersion` integration tests (§4) — these two functions carry the reproducibility and audit-integrity guarantees the whole paper's premise depends on.\n5. API route auth/validation tests (§5) — cheap, catches the highest-consequence class of bug (an unprotected write path).\n6. Engine TDD skeletons (§1b) — write now, they'll fail (`NotImplementedError`) until Phase 2/3, then start passing as you build — this is the eval-harness-alongside-the-engine discipline `AGENTS.md` asks for.",
        "level": 2
      }
    ],
